WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.240
A pilot on an early
morning flight over

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.520
eastern France captures
this image.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.060
It looks like a city at
night with all of the

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:09.890
street lights
illuminating all the

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:11.130
roads and houses.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:14.090
Closer examination of the
image reveals something

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:14.960
strange.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.100
You can see rows of
flames that have erupted

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.140
all the way across this
vast area in France.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.230
But why?

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.630
The aerial image has
captured a strange

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.000
technique the farmers
employ to save their

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.350
livelihoods from ruin.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.260
Farmers lined their
fields with torches and

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.550
then light them so that
these little fires.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.570
Right next to the grapes
are able to warm up the

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:43.000
air right around the
grapes and prevent the

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:43.530
frost.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.520
But it's actually not the
heat of the torches

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.070
themselves. That's the
primary factor to keeping

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:49.300
the crops safe.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:51.250
It's the smoke that's
the critical thing.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.250
The smoke acts like
almost a layer of clouds,

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.100
like a fog that traps
the heat of the earth

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.030
from getting out into
space.

